<section class="mp-section" id="buyers"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">01 / Match the product to the decision</p><h2>HR software is a category.<br>The buyer has a specific job.</h2><p>A payroll platform, recruiting tool and competency system need different account criteria and conversations. Begin with the process your software can credibly improve.</p></div>
<p class="gp-scroll-hint">Scroll the table horizontally on smaller screens.</p><div class="gp-table-wrap" role="region" aria-labelledby="hr-buyers-caption" tabindex="0"><table class="gp-table"><caption id="hr-buyers-caption">Illustrative buyer mapping for HR technology campaigns</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Software workflow</th><th scope="col">Roles to investigate</th><th scope="col">A useful demonstration should establish</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Payroll and HR operations</th><td>Payroll leadership, HR Operations and Finance; HRIS or IT when systems are involved.</td><td>How inputs, approvals, exceptions and corrections would work in the current environment.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Recruiting technology</th><td>Talent Acquisition, recruiting operations and hiring managers, with HR technology support as needed.</td><td>Which part of the recruiting workflow changes and who remains responsible for decisions.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Training and competency software</th><td>Learning, quality, compliance or operating leaders, according to the product.</td><td>How role requirements, qualifications, evidence and retraining are managed.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Workforce analytics or frontline software</th><td>People analytics, HR, operations and relevant system owners.</td><td>Which employee population, decision or operating process the software supports.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Choose the roles that match your product. A CHRO may sponsor the purchase while a specialist leads the evaluation. Exclude companies where product coverage, implementation requirements or commercial fit do not match.</p><p>For outreach beyond HR technology, explore <a href="/services/saas-appointment-setting/">SaaS appointment setting and demo booking</a>.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="campaign"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">02 / From account selection to sales context</p><h2>Build a campaign around<br>a reason to evaluate.</h2><p>A list of HR titles does not explain why someone should take a meeting. The preparation and conversation need to work together.</p></div><div class="mp-scope-grid">
<article><span class="mp-step">Prepare the market</span><h3>Choose the accounts and the question.</h3><p>Define company fit, workforce context, territories, buying roles and exclusions. Review existing accounts or scope fresh research and data. Approve the product claims and conversation approach before outreach.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Campaign brief</strong>An agreed audience and product-specific calling brief.</p></article>
<article><span class="mp-step">Work the conversation</span><h3>Listen beyond the first objection.</h3><p>A human caller asks about the relevant process, finds the responsible person and agrees suitable follow-up. “We already have an HRIS” can lead to a workflow question; it can also establish that the account is not a fit.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Call notes</strong>Confirmed context, a referral, a next action or a clear disqualification.</p></article>
<article><span class="mp-step">Prepare the demonstration</span><h3>Give the seller a useful starting point.</h3><p>Qualify the purpose and participants, agree the appointment and transfer the notes. Keep unconfirmed budget, system or purchasing details visible so the demo team knows what to establish.</p><p class="mp-output"><strong>Demo handoff</strong>A meeting with an agenda and the information behind it.</p></article>
</div><p class="mp-caption">A new HR leader, expansion or system initiative can justify research. Confirm the need, budget and project status in conversation.</p>
<div class="mp-tool-band"><div><h3>Put your software offer into a campaign brief.</h3><p>Explore an audience, calling approach and relevant resources before agreeing the managed work.</p></div><a class="mp-button" href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">See How We’d Run Your Campaign ↗</a></div>
</div></section>

<section class="mp-section" id="demo-standard"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">03 / Agree what qualifies</p><h2>Give buyers a reason<br>to attend the demo.</h2><p>Before outreach, define what your sellers need to know and which missing facts would make a meeting premature. Apply the standard to the actual conversation.</p><ul class="gp-checklist"><li><strong>Account and role:</strong> the organization fits and the participant has a relevant responsibility.</li><li><strong>Current situation:</strong> the prospect explains a process, constraint or priority your product can address.</li><li><strong>Reason to continue:</strong> there is a credible purpose and suitable timing for the discussion.</li><li><strong>Demo design:</strong> the participants understand what the session should establish.</li><li><strong>Open questions:</strong> the handoff distinguishes confirmed facts from details still needing discovery.</li></ul><p>Track bookings, attendance, sales acceptance and opportunities separately with the <a href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Meeting Quality Check</a>. A product demonstration and a qualified sales opportunity are different stages.</p></div>
<aside class="mp-note"><p class="mp-label">Illustrative HR software handoff</p><h3>Show the process.<br>Keep the unknowns.</h3><dl><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Quality leader responsible for qualification records.</dd></div><div><dt>Current process</dt><dd>Training and role evidence are held in separate records.</dd></div><div><dt>Demo purpose</dt><dd>Review how requirements and supporting evidence could be connected.</dd></div><div><dt>Participants</dt><dd>Quality lead, with a learning-system colleague to be confirmed.</dd></div><div><dt>Still unknown</dt><dd>Integration requirements, budget and purchasing timetable.</dd></div></dl><p class="mp-small">Fictional example. It illustrates the fields, not a client conversation or reported result.</p></aside></div></section>

<section class="mp-section mp-proof" id="hr-proof"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div class="gp-proof-copy"><p class="mp-kicker">04 / Published workforce software evidence</p><h2>Nine booked demos.<br>Two proposals.<br>In the first 90 days.</h2><p>The provider sold workforce training, competency and qualification software. Outreach covered medical-device companies, healthcare organizations and manufacturers, with messaging adapted to each buyer’s responsibilities.</p><p>The campaign focused on who was qualified to do the work and how the organization could demonstrate it. That context made the software easier to discuss than a broad feature pitch.</p><p>These were booked demos. The case does not report attendance, signed customers or revenue. It describes one engagement; outcomes vary.</p></div><aside class="gp-stat-block" aria-label="HR software case result"><p class="mp-label">First campaign period / client identity withheld</p><h3>Read the work behind the figures.</h3><div class="gp-stats"><div><strong>9</strong><span>booked product demos</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>proposals</span></div><div><strong>90</strong><span>campaign days</span></div></div><p>The full case explains the company type, buyer context, approach and limits of the reported result.</p><a class="mp-button" href="/case-studies/hr-software-lead-generation/">Read the HR Software Case Study ↗</a></aside></div></section>

<section class="mp-section" id="investment"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">05 / Investment and responsibilities</p><h2>Scope the market,<br>the preparation and the calls.</h2><p class="mp-price">From US$4,000<span> / month</span></p><p>The starting managed programme assumes a defined B2B offer, target market, usable accounts or contacts, CRM and calendar access, and sellers ready to handle qualified conversations.</p><p>Fresh prospect research, licensed data, additional markets and greater capacity affect the fee. Most programmes begin with an initial three-month engagement. <a href="/pricing/">Review the full starting assumptions and pricing</a>.</p><p>You provide approved product evidence, qualification requirements, timely feedback and people to run the demos. CallTeam manages the outreach work agreed in the proposal.</p></div><aside class="mp-tool"><p class="mp-label">Is your team ready?</p><h3>Be ready to<br>show the product.</h3><p>A focused offer, clear account criteria and a sales team able to progress interest make the campaign easier to operate. Qualification cannot repair an unsupported product claim or an unavailable demo team.</p><p>Want to see who does the live work? Explore <a href="/human-led-appointment-setting/">human-led appointment setting</a>. Need a wider front-of-sales function? See <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">outsourced SDR services</a>.</p></aside></div></section>

<section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="resources"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">Prepare the conversation</p><h2>Use the HR sales resources<br>behind the campaign.</h2><p>The guides explain the method; this service puts an agreed team behind execution. Choose the resource for the product and decision you are working on.</p></div><ul class="gp-resource-list"><li><a href="/articles/hr-technology-outbound-sales-playbook/">HR technology outbound sales playbook →</a><span>Account selection, workforce context, messaging and campaign planning.</span></li><li><a href="/articles/chro-outbound-sales-playbook/">CHRO outbound sales playbook →</a><span>Frame an executive conversation around a workforce decision.</span></li><li><a href="/articles/sell-hr-technology-without-leading-ai/">Sell HR technology through the use case →</a><span>Explain the operating outcome before introducing an AI capability.</span></li><li><a href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/payroll-software-cold-call-script-hr-operations/">Payroll software cold call script →</a><span>Prepare an HR Operations conversation about payroll work.</span></li><li><a href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/workforce-analytics-software-cold-call-script-chros/">Workforce analytics cold call script →</a><span>Connect the data conversation to a decision the buyer owns.</span></li></ul></div></section>
